567	     * Rejects a new owner whose derived identity key is already used by any existing owner. All
568	     * duplicate detection is consolidated into this single key (see
569	     * {@link Owner#identityKey(String, String, String)}): the normalized E.164 telephone, the
570	     * canonical (trimmed, lower-cased) email and the household identifier the owner would receive,
571	     * joined by {@code '|'}. The submitted telephone and email have already been normalized in
572	     * place, and the household identifier is the value {@link #assignHousehold} would later store
573	     * (see {@link #prospectiveHouseholdId(OwnerFieldsDto)}). An owner is a duplicate only when its
574	     * whole key equals an existing owner's, so a difference in any part — for example two members
575	     * of one household with different telephones — yields distinct keys and is allowed. When a
576	     * match is found a {@link DuplicateIdentityException} is thrown, which the exception advice
577	     * renders as a 409 Conflict response.
